# A download Chromium has gone quiet about stays running (GitHub #895). ${TRICKLE} sends the first
# 64 KB of a 10 MB file and holds the rest; closing the tab that started it leaves the profile with
# no page for the engine to report it to, so nothing comes for longer than the watchdog's 5 s. With
# Safe Browsing on, the engine writes it to "Unconfirmed <n>.crdownload", neither the file nor
# <file>.crdownload: the watchdog read that as cancelled, and the row said Cancelled while the
# download carried on. A page in the profile again, its reports come back, and it is cancelled
# from its row, so the quit doesn't ask "Downloads in progress".
# promise: #895
home
budget rss=600 stalls50=5
cra://open?url=${TRICKLE}/quiet.bin
wait 2
cra://debug?downloadState=started
expect-log download state started: running=true progress=0.007 rows=\["66 KB of 10 MB
cra://action/closeTab
wait 10
cra://debug?downloadState=quiet
expect-log download state quiet: running=true progress=0.007 rows=\["66 KB of 10 MB
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=after-quiet
wait 2
cra://debug?download=cancel
expect-log download control: cancel
wait 1
cra://debug?downloadState=cancelled
expect-log download state cancelled: running=false progress=none rows=\["Cancelled"\]
